{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Only there shall be no needy one among you.</b> And below it says ״כִּי לֹא יֶחְדַּל אֶבְיוֹן מִקֶּרֶב הָאָרֶץ״, and our Sages of blessed memory said (Sifrei Re'eh 132): this one is in the time when they do the will of the Place, that one is in the time when they do not do His will. And the witness to this is what is stated: ״אֶפֶס כִּי לֹא יִהְיֶה בְךָ אֶבְיוֹן וְגוֹ׳ רַק אִם שָׁמוֹעַ תִּשְׁמַע בְּקוֹל ה׳״ — meaning, solely and only on this condition: if you will indeed obey. But what they said regarding the verse ״כִּי לֹא יֶחְדַּל אֶבְיוֹן מִקֶּרֶב הָאָרֶץ״ requires explanation: what is the indication that this verse speaks of a time when they do not do His will? And further, it is difficult: what is the giving of a reason in his saying ״עַל כֵּן אָנֹכִי מְצַוְּךָ פָּתוֹחַ תִּפְתַּח״ — what does this come to teach us? It is obvious that if there is no poor person, to whom would one give? And further, it is difficult: why did he begin the passage ״כִּי יִהְיֶה בְךָ אֶבְיוֹן וְגוֹ׳ בְּאַרְצְךָ״ — but surely charity is a personal obligation and applies even outside the Land. And likewise he concludes the passage: ״וּלְאֶבְיוֹנְךָ בְּאַרְצֶךָ״, and in the verse ״כִּי לֹא יֶחְדַּל״ he said ״מִקֶּרֶב הָאָרֶץ״ and did not say ״מִקֶּרֶב אַרְצְךָ״." "Rather, surely this is its explanation: all the poor of your land take precedence over the poor of outside the Land, and the entire passage speaks of a time when they do His will, as is clear from the language ״רַק אִם שָׁמוֹעַ״ etc. And when it says ״כִּי יִהְיֶה בְךָ אֶבְיוֹן מֵאַחַד אַחֶיךָ בְּאַחַד שְׁעָרֶיךָ בְּאַרְצְךָ״, all these singular forms of אֶחָד point to the fact that in the time when Israel do the will of the Place, blessed be He, then no needy one would be found there except one from a city and one from a family — and that is entirely uncommon. And when it says ״כִּי לֹא יֶחְדַּל אֶבְיוֹן מִקֶּרֶב הָאָרֶץ״, it speaks of outside the Land, and that is in a time when they do not do His will, since they did not ascend to the land of Israel with their brothers, as happened in the days of Ezra, when the majority did not ascend from Babylonia. And there ״לֹא יֶחְדַּל אֶבְיוֹן מִקֶּרֶב הָאָרֶץ״ — that is, from the midst of the land at large, and therefore it does not say ״אַרְצְךָ״. And the entire verse ״כִּי לֹא יֶחְדַּל אֶבְיוֹן״ is a resolution of the first verse, which said ״כִּי יִהְיֶה בְךָ אֶבְיוֹן וְגוֹ׳ בְּאַרְצְךָ״ — why did it use ״בְּאַרְצְךָ״, when surely this commandment applies also outside the Land? To this it says, as if responding: ״כִּי לֹא יֶחְדַּל אֶבְיוֹן מִקֶּרֶב הָאָרֶץ״ — that is, outside the Land. And you might be inclined to say: since the poor of outside the Land come to you from a far land, it is not fitting to turn them away and they should take precedence over the poor of your land — ״עַל כֵּן אָנֹכִי מְצַוְּךָ פָּתוֹחַ תִּפְתַּח אֶת יָדְךָ לַעֲנִיֶּךָ וּלְאֶבְיוֹנְךָ בְּאַרְצֶךָ״, meaning: therefore I said to you above ״בְּאַרְצְךָ״ — to decree that the law is with the poor of your land, that they take precedence over the poor of outside the Land, who are מִקֶּרֶב הָאָרֶץ." "And what he said, ״עַל כֵּן אָנֹכִי מְצַוְּךָ לֵאמֹר״ — for speaking is the essence and is better than giving, since the one who gives a coin to a poor person is blessed with six blessings, but the one who comforts him with words — with eleven blessings (Bava Batra 9b). And this is ״לֵאמֹר״ to him words of appeasement and comfort. And there are those who say ״לֵאמֹר פָּתֹחַ תִּפְתַּח״ — that one should also urge others regarding charity and say to them ״פָּתֹחַ תִּפְתַּח״ etc."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {0 "ה׳ expanded as standard; 'the Place' (המקום) retained literally as a divine epithet.", 1 "The final phrase 'who are מִקֶּרֶב הָאָרֶץ' reads literally 'who are from the midst of the land (at large),' contrasting אַרְצְךָ (your land) with הָאָרֶץ (the land in general, i.e., outside the Land of Israel).", 2 "The Talmudic citation 'ב״ב ט:' resolved to Bava Batra 9b based on the well-known passage about blessings for charity."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:12:40.371380186Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}